> =E5=9C=A8 2023-01-03=E6=98=9F=E6=9C=9F=E4=BA=8C=E7=9A=84 01:17 +0000=EF=
=BC=8CAndre Przywara=E5=86=99=E9=81=93=EF=BC=9A
> > The Allwinner R528/T113-s/D1/D1s SoCs all share the same die, so use
> > the
> > same DRAM initialisation code.
> > Make use of prior art here and lift some code from awboot[1], which
> > carried init code based on earlier decompilation efforts, but with a
> > GPL2 license tag.
> > This code has been heavily reworked and cleaned up, to match previous
> > DRAM routines for other SoCs, and also to be closer to U-Boot's
> > coding
> > style and support routines.
> > The actual DRAM chip timing parameters are included in the main file,
> > since they cover all DRAM types, and are protected by a new Kconfig
> > CONFIG_SUNXI_DRAM_TYPE symbol, which allows the compiler to pick only
> > the relevant settings, at build time.
> >=20
> > The relevant DRAM chips/board specific configuration parameters are
> > delivered via Kconfig, so this code here should work for all
> > supported
> > SoCs and DRAM chips combinations. =20
>=20
> The D1 DRAM controller should be similar to the R329 one, which I added
> (legacy) support at [1].

Thanks for the hint (and apologies for not replying to your comment
on IRC before).

So this one here is clearly an RFC. I found myself deeply in a "let
me fix this comment formatting" rabbit hole lately, so wanted to get this
out now, so that people can start looking at it. That's why I didn't
compare your driver with that code here yet. From a very brief look, yours
is much more compact, so there is indeed some hope the two can get merged.
But I doubt that I realistically find the time in the next weeks to
compare them carefully. Also this driver here has clearly some work left
(for instance naming all the registers).

So any help, contributions and comments to this topic are warmly welcomed.

Cheers,
Andre

